## Rules and AUDIT

Rules in `docs/rules/` are organized into three tiers:
- **Application rules**: `docs/rules/{{APP_NAME}}.md` (this repository's own rules and overrides)
- **Stack rules**: `docs/rules/dotnet.md`, plus every .NET facet rule file under `docs/rules/` (e.g., `dotnet-client.md`) (managed by dev-standards)
- **Shared rules**: Universal engineering standards (`docs/rules/standard.md`, `docs/rules/documentation.md`, `docs/rules/specs.md`, `docs/rules/testing.md`), plus every conditional shared rule file under `docs/rules/` (managed by dev-standards)

**Precedence on conflict**: Application rules > Stack rules > Shared rules.

- **Rule Scope**: which rule files and specification every change complies with — and when to report missing conditional shared rule domains — is stated in `docs/rules/standard.md` (How to Use These Rules). The specification of {{APP_NAME}} is `docs/specs/{{APP_NAME}}.md`.
- **Loading Rules**: Read this file, every applicable file under `docs/rules/`, `docs/specs/{{APP_NAME}}.md`, and `docs/references/code-map.md` before writing code (including when transitioning from a plan to implementation).
- **Completion Gate (AUDIT)**: Before reporting an implementation task as complete, pass the AUDIT gate in `docs/rules/standard.md`.
- **File Ownership**: rule files under `docs/rules/` managed by dev-standards are copies of its pinned tag; repository- and application-specific rules are maintained in `docs/rules/{{APP_NAME}}.md`.

